VERSION 5.8 ;
DESIGN bias_gen ;
UNITS DISTANCE MICRONS 1000 ;

# A small analog bias-generator block. Three routed nets exercise the cases an
# analog layout cares about (and a digital std-cell block rarely shows so cleanly):
#
#   vbias    — a long, thin bias distribution line (met1): resistance matters, runs
#              parallel to a sensitive node so it couples to it.
#   vsense   — a high-impedance sensitive node carried up the stack (met1 -> via ->
#              met2): low cap is the whole point, and it must not pick up noise from
#              the bias line running alongside it.
#   vsupply  — a wide local supply tap (met3): low R by design, big grounded cap.
#
# Geometry is in DEF DB units (1000/um). Coordinates chosen so the RC is hand-checkable.

NETS 3 ;
- vbias ( mirror X ) ( cascode G ) ( load G )
  + ROUTED met1 ( 1000 1000 ) ( 1000 21000 ) ;
- vsense ( ota OUT ) ( comp INP )
  + ROUTED met1 ( 2000 1000 ) ( 2000 11000 )
    NEW met2 ( 2000 11000 ) M1M2_VIA ( 12000 11000 ) ;
- vsupply ( tap0 VDD ) ( tap1 VDD )
  + ROUTED met3 ( 1000 25000 ) M2M3_VIA ( 31000 25000 ) ;
END NETS

END DESIGN
